Level 3 par: Promises (The Savior).🤝
Promise Kya Hota Hai? (Asli Matlab)Real life ki tarah, 
JavaScript mein bhi Promise ka matlab ek vaada hi hai.Maan lo tumne Swiggy se khana order kiya. 
Jaise hi tum order karte ho, Swiggy tumhein ek Promise de deta hai ki tumhara khana aayega.Jab tak khana ban raha hai aur delivery boy raste mein hai,
us Promise ka status hota hai: Pending.Agar khana sahi-salamat tum tak pahunch gaya, toh Promise poora ho gaya: Fulfilled (Resolved).Agar beech raste mein delivery boy ka accident ho gaya ya restaurant band mila, 
toh Promise toot gaya: Rejected.Node.js/JavaScript mein bhi exact yahi cheez hoti hai jab hum database se data nikalte hain ya file read karte hain.🛠️ Promise Ka Syntax (Anatomy)Ek Promise do cheezein leta hai apne andar: 
resolve (kaam pakka hone par chalane ke liye) aur reject (error aane par chalane ke liye).


Chalo ek simple Promise banakar dekhte hain jo kisi database se user ka data laane ka natak (simulate) karega:JavaScriptconst checkUserInDB = (userId) => {
  // Hum naya Promise return kar rahe hain
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    console.log("🔍 Database mein user dhoodha jaa raha hai...");

    // 2 second ka fake network delay
    setTimeout(() => {
      const userFound = true; // Isko false karke bhi test karenge

      if (userFound) {
        // Agar user mil gaya, toh data ke saath resolve kar do
        resolve({ id: userId, name: "Mehtab", status: "Active" });
      } else {
        // Agar gadbad hui, toh error ke saath reject kar do
        reject("❌ Error: User database mein nahi mila!");
      }
    }, 2000);
  });
};
🚀 Promise Ko Use Kaise Karte Hain? 
(.then aur .catch)Upar jo function humne banaya hai, wo ek Promise return karta hai. Uska data nikalne ke liye hum do tools ka use karte hain:.then() $\rightarrow$ Agar promise resolve hua, toh ye chalega..catch() $\rightarrow$ Agar promise reject hua, toh ye chalega.JavaScript// Function ko call kiya
checkUserInDB("USER_101")
  .then((userData) => {
    // resolve() ka data yahan userData mein aayega
    console.log("🎉 Promise Fulfilled! User ka data mila:", userData);
  })
  .catch((error) => {
    // reject() ka message yahan error mein aayega
    console.log("😢 Promise Broken! Wajah:", error);
  });
🧠 Output Kaise Aayega?
Pehle turant print hoga: 🔍 Database mein user dhoodha jaa raha hai...Server freeze nahi hoga, 
baaki kaam chalte rahenge.Thik 2 second baad, screen par aayega: 🎉 Promise Fulfilled! User ka data mila: { id: 'USER_101', name: 'Mehtab', status: 'Active' }
